 ## Remark
 
+For the Hessian comparison below, assume additionally that the residual map $r$ is $C^2$ on an open neighborhood of the point under discussion; the experimental-design model itself requires only $C^1$.
+
 For the unweighted nonlinear least-squares objective $\phi(\theta)=\tfrac12\|r(\theta)\|_2^2$, the matrix $J(\theta)^TJ(\theta)$ is the Gauss–Newton term of the Hessian. The exact identity is
 $$\nabla^2\phi(\theta)=J(\theta)^TJ(\theta)+\sum_i r_i(\theta)\nabla^2r_i(\theta)$$
 by [[thm-nonlinear-least-squares-gradient-and-hessian]]. Thus the two matrices agree at zero residual, but the information matrix defined in [[def-nonlinear-experimental-design-and-local-identifiability]] is not asserted to be the full Hessian at a nonzero-residual point.
